#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1035 expect=skipped domain=DS
#note "THE DSCAT ALL-FACET GATE (Fix #331 bucket 2, M2-D24 / M3-D18; pin owed by review S9 and authored by Fix #340). The DS dataset deliberately declares no DSCAT column, so Requirements.Variables.All [DSCAT] rejects the dataset and the rule is SKIPPED naming DSCAT. Remove the All entry and the rule EXECUTES: since Fix #330 retired the injected var_exists guard, a bare empty(DSCAT) is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing) and nothing else in the Check restricts the rows, so it would fire on EVERY row -- the flood the gate exists for. If this scenario EXECUTES (violation or silent pass), the gate has been removed -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | COMPLETED | COMPLETED
